<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21216] ldiskfs: empty prealloc_table makes mballoc allocate over fs metadata</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21216</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;An OST whose mballoc preallocation table is empty (&lt;tt&gt;echo 0 &amp;gt; /proc/fs/ldiskfs/&amp;lt;dev&amp;gt;/prealloc_table&lt;/tt&gt;, which &lt;tt&gt;ext4_mb_check_and_update_prealloc()&lt;/tt&gt; accepts) aborts its journal when a write lands beyond the blocks already allocated to a file:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;LDISKFS-fs error (device dm-1): ldiskfs_mb_mark_diskspace_used:3476: comm ll_ost_io00_005: Allocating blocks 1297408-1048576 which overlap fs metadata
Aborting journal on device dm-1-8.
LDISKFS-fs (dm-1): Remounting filesystem read-only
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With errors=panic the OSS panics, and the OST needs e2fsck before it can be mounted again.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In &lt;tt&gt;ext4_mb_normalize_request()&lt;/tt&gt; as modified by ext4-prealloc.patch, an empty table leaves both &lt;tt&gt;wind&lt;/tt&gt; and &lt;tt&gt;last_non_zero&lt;/tt&gt; at 0, so neither branch sets the goal: &lt;tt&gt;start&lt;/tt&gt; stays 0 and &lt;tt&gt;size&lt;/tt&gt; stays the file size in blocks. The normalized goal then does not necessarily contain the requested blocks and can be larger than a block group. The patch also removes &lt;tt&gt;BUG_ON(size &amp;gt; EXT4_BLOCKS_PER_GROUP(sb))&lt;/tt&gt;, so mballoc allocates a range that runs into the next group's metadata. This code came with &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12335" title="mb_prealloc_table  table read/write code is racy" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-12335"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-12335&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (fixed size preallocation table); before that, an empty table caused the divide error of &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-3719" title="divide error in ldiskfs_mb_normalize_request on MDT" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-3719"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-3719&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Every ext4-prealloc.patch variant in master has it (RHEL 8/9/10, SLES 15, Ubuntu and mainline series), as does every release since 2.13 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12335" title="mb_prealloc_table  table read/write code is racy" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-12335"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-12335&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproducer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;OSTCOUNT=1 OSTSIZE=6000000 bash llmount.sh
echo 0 &amp;gt; /proc/fs/ldiskfs/&amp;lt;ost dev&amp;gt;/prealloc_table
dd &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;=/dev/zero bs=500M count=1 of=/mnt/lustre/file3
sync
dd &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt;=/dev/zero seek=100k bs=16k count=1 of=/mnt/lustre/file3
sync
OSTCOUNT=1 bash llmountcleanup.sh
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Without the fix the console shows the error above and the node may crash.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: when the table is empty, do not normalize the request; use the original logical start and length, as stock ext4 does for requests it does not normalize. This was seen on HPE ClusterStor OSS nodes and is fixed in the HPE Lustre branches (HPE ticket LUS-12766).&lt;/p&gt;</description>
